# lf config for zide's picker pane.
#
# Read via `lf -config <this file>` (see bin/zide-pick): lf has NO
# LF_CONFIG_HOME — it only looks at /etc/lf/lfrc and ~/.config/lf/lfrc — so
# -config is the one way to point it at a file here.
#
# Why lf rather than yazi: the picker pane is 40 columns
# (layouts/default.kdl `filepicker size=40`). yazi's layout is a static
# `[mgr] ratio` with no width awareness, and the plugin that used to adapt it
# (auto-layout.yazi) hooked `Tab:layout()`, an API yazi >= 25 removed — on
# current yazi it does not error, it silently paints an EMPTY pane. lf's
# on-redraw sees the terminal width, so this pane can adapt for real.
#
# How `set ratios` behaves (lf(1)): the NUMBER OF ITEMS is the number of
# panes, and with `preview` on the rightmost item is the preview width. A
# single-pane view therefore needs `set preview false` AND a one-item ratios.
#
# Two traps, both hit while writing this:
#  1. lf runs these bodies with `sh -c` and exports only a fixed set of vars
#     (f, fs, fx, id, PWD, …). An `lf` that is merely on the parent PATH is NOT
#     guaranteed to resolve here — when it failed, every redraw printed
#     "lf: command not found" and the pane stayed at lf's stock 1:2:3.
#     So: this file uses @lf@, which the flake substitutes for the absolute
#     store path at build time (substituteInPlace in flake.nix). Do NOT use
#     %lf% here — inside a `cmd` body it expands to an empty string, which
#     turns every call into `-remote ...` (i.e. runs the current directory).
#  2. `lf -remote` talks to the server over a socket, and `on-redraw` fires on
#     every screen refresh — keep it to at most two remote calls per branch.

cmd on-redraw %{{
    if [ $lf_width -le 40 ]; then
        @lf@ -remote "send $id set preview false"
        @lf@ -remote "send $id set ratios 1"
    elif [ $lf_width -le 80 ]; then
        @lf@ -remote "send $id set preview true"
        @lf@ -remote "send $id set ratios 1:2"
    else
        @lf@ -remote "send $id set preview true"
        @lf@ -remote "send $id set ratios 1:2:3"
    fi
}}
